        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add Temporal Alignment paper]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/papers-we-love/papers-we-love/pull/801</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/papers-we-love/papers-we-love/pull/801"/>
        <updated>2024-10-02T09:40:53.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/660353?u=7b5ae3467a6532c9a47179bcbd826a8d20fff2a4&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h2 dir="auto">Paper Title:</h2>
<p dir="auto">Temporal Alignment</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Paper Year:</h3>
<p dir="auto">2012</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Reasons for including paper</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Defining a temporal version for each operator of Codd's relational algebra is a big improvement on existing temporal data techniques. It puts temporal data on a solid mathematical foundation by integrating it into relational theory. It solves the composability problems found in TSQL2 and SQL:2011.</li>
<li>The authors demonstrated the practicality of their approach by patching PostgreSQL and benchmarking their new functionality vs a pure-SQL alternative.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
